<title>AUSTRIA: UAE SEES ROLLOVER AS MOST LIKELY OPEC OUTCOME.</title>
<headline>UAE SEES ROLLOVER AS MOST LIKELY OPEC OUTCOME.</headline>
<dateline>VIENNA 1997-06-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>United Arab Emirates' oil minister Obaid bin Saif al-Nasseri said on Monday he thought the most likely outcome of this week's OPEC meeting would be a rollover of current quotas.</p>
<p>&quot;I think this is what will happen,&quot; he told reporters.</p>
<p>He also said that concern about current price levels was justified but added &quot;they are not that low&quot;.</p>
<p>North Sea Brent Blend crude prices have fallen from around $25 per barrel earlier this year to just below $18 now.</p>
<p>-- Vienna newsroom +431 713 2002</p>
</text>
